 $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." 13194139535908 true] [17592186373949 1113 #uuid "472a84d4-71fc-53d1-84b9-c9c734ba9c9f" 13194139535908 true] [17592186373949 1145 "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-(3+s)}{[{e}^{-(3+s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-4{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" 13194139535908 true] [17592186373950 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373951 13194139535908 true] [17592186373950 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373952 13194139535908 true] [17592186373950 1000 #edb/ref 17592186